# fd-ignore — paths fd and fzf should never descend into.
#
# gitignore syntax. Used via `fd --ignore-file "$ZDOTDIR/fd-ignore"`.
#
# This replaces the old FD_EXCLUDES variable, which joined an array of
# "--exclude foo" strings into one scalar. That only ever worked where the
# value was re-parsed by a shell (inside FZF_DEFAULT_COMMAND, or an `eval`):
# zsh does not word-split unquoted parameters, so passing $FD_EXCLUDES
# straight to fd sent it a single giant argument. A real ignore file has no
# quoting or splitting problems at all.

